# Teardown on a really founded camp with a disclosed synthetic labour crew: real
# KingdomCommission.Commission, real KingdomMaterials.OrderStrike, exact salvage by strike
# receipt (fire = the zero-salvage boundary, larder = the positive one), and a negative
# second-strike order that must refuse by name.
#
# SYNTHETIC SETUP, DISCLOSED: the camp is founded and the water dedicated by the harness, a
# 2-body labour crew is enrolled through the real KingdomCitizenship.TryEnroll +
# KingdomResidents.TryEnsureRow pair (crew size 2 = RaisingHandsWanted, the minimum that
# saturates construction effectiveness), and each design's own authored bill (read live from
# RuntimeData/KingdomBuildings.xml, never hardcoded) is minted as N separate single-unit
# fixture bodies per material into a per-case dedicated stockpile, bounded by that store's own
# declared capacity. Nothing forces KingdomBuilt, the job phase or the strike receipt.
# Not ordinary play, not a rendered Charter, no save/load and no cold-load claim.
#
# Four checks, cumulative ticks 2400/6000/9600/13200 (deltas 2400/3600/3600/3600), widened per
# review-bba51c4-teardown-findings.md nit 1 from the prior zero-slack 2000/4800/7600/10800: the
# first attended settlement pass after founding prices a freshly-selected raising at 0 (Assign
# selects on that same pass, before any labour is priced against it), so the first interval is
# TWO 1200-tick passes -- the second is what actually prices fire's 600 ticks -- and every later
# interval keeps one full spare pass over the 1200-tick legs it covers (fire's removal/salvage,
# larder's own raise+strike, larder's removal). Fire and larder are SEQUENCED, one gang at a
# time (Frame.Check() commissions larder only once fire reaches Phase 2), never concurrent.
#
# FIXTURE CREW DO NOT WANDER, DISCLOSED: once kept off a raising's footprint, a crew body is
# pinned stationary (Brain.Wanders=false, Brain.WandersRandomly=false, Brain.Stay(cell), the
# exact production idiom for anchoring an NPC) so it cannot WANDER back onto the footprint on
# its own between the four scripted checks. A real settlement's own wandering residents are
# never anchored this way and can still trigger issue #163 (a living occupant permanently
# blocking an authored ground-layer slot); that production gap is being closed separately, on
# fix/034-apply-occupant-announce.
#
# review-5093b00-teardown-findings.md item 2, DISCLOSED, NOT FIXED: Brain.Stay only stops
# wandering -- it stops neither this body's own construction LABOUR (posting/hands are
# property-driven off KingdomConstructionPresence, never off Brain) nor PRODUCTION itself:
# KingdomStations.Claim re-issues Stay(target) plus a MoveTo(target) goal for a posted body,
# target being the works cell or an adjacent one, so a construction-posted crew body is walked
# BACK onto the footprint by production's own posting. This fixture cannot keep a site clear by
# construction; #163 may still fire. A GREEN teardown run is owed to the #163 production fix
# (settler displacement at apply), not to this mitigation.
#
# KNOWN GAP, DISCLOSED, NOT FIXED: the crew has no home plot, so a roofless departure brink
# (KingdomLodgingRules.GraceDays = 6 days = 7200 ticks from the warned tick) may fire near
# tick 8400-9600, inside this budget and before the final check. Departure is not frozen or
# synthesized away; if it happens first, Frame.Check() re-Requires the real production crew
# count (KingdomResidents.OnRollCount) and refuses by a named outcome, "case=<fire|larder>
# outcome=crew-departed onRoll=<n> wanted=<CrewSize> tick=<t>", inside the same Fail()
# envelope every other named refusal in this scenario uses -- a named REFUSED verb, never a
# silently stalled incomplete case and never a false pass.
DESCRIPTION=a really built camp fire and larder are struck on real turns, return exactly the computed salvage, and refuse a second strike
REQUEST=founding-first-city
START=8.22@40,12
SCRIPT=stagedigest;teardown-setup;advance 2400;teardown-check;advance 3600;teardown-check;advance 3600;teardown-check;advance 3600;teardown-check;stagedigest
VERBS=teardown-setup,teardown-check
EXPECT=stagedigest:OK~founded=false,teardown-setup:OK~fire=1,advance:OK,teardown-check:OK~native-teardown,advance:OK,teardown-check:OK~native-teardown,advance:OK,teardown-check:OK~native-teardown,advance:OK,teardown-check:OK~cases=2 passed=2 failed=0,stagedigest:OK~founded=true,COMPLETE
SET=materials,growth,native-regression
TIMEOUT=1200
